  id: camel
  displayName: Camel
  styleLabel: Slow & tanky
  description: The camel is a tall desert animal with one big hump. The hump stores
    fat, so a camel can travel a long way without food. Its wide feet walk easily
    on soft sand.
  history: For thousands of years, people in Arabia travelled the desert on camels.
    Camel caravans carried frankincense, spices and trade goods between faraway towns.
    Bedouin families also drank camel milk and made cloth from its hair.
